1.Explain why RNN is widely used in Natural Language Processing.

RNN designed to handle sequential data, making it suitable for NLP tasks where the order of words matters/
Why RNN ?
1.Capture word sequence - Sentence meaning depends on word order
Eg. Dog bites man. --> Man bites dog Same word  different meanings
2.Maintains memory of previous words
RNN uses a hidden state to remember earlier information
Useful for understanding context
3.Handles variable length input
Sentences can have different number of words
4.Suitable for NLP tasks
Sentiment Analysis, Text classification,Speech Recognition

Eg. I don't like movie RNN remember not while reading later words, helping correct sentiment.

